sequenceDiagram
    participant "Reading Module" as ReadingModule
    participant "Primary Database" as PrimaryDatabase
    participant "Infrastructure (MediatR)" as InfrastructureMediatR
    participant "Engagement Module" as EngagementModule
    participant "Recommendations Module" as RecommendationsModule

    activate ReadingModule
    ReadingModule->>ReadingModule: 1. Handles LogReadingSessionCommand
    ReadingModule->>PrimaryDatabase: 2. Begin Database Transaction
    PrimaryDatabase-->>ReadingModule: Transaction object
    ReadingModule->>PrimaryDatabase: 3. INSERT INTO ReadingSession
    PrimaryDatabase-->>ReadingModule: New Session ID
    ReadingModule->>ReadingModule: 4. Raise ReadingSessionLogged event
    ReadingModule->>PrimaryDatabase: 5. Commit Transaction
    PrimaryDatabase-->>ReadingModule: Success confirmation
    ReadingModule->>InfrastructureMediatR: 6. Publish ReadingSessionLogged event
    ReadingModule->>ReadingModule: 7. Return 200 OK API Response
    ReadingModule-->>ReadingModule: JSON payload with new Session ID
    activate EngagementModule
    InfrastructureMediatR->>EngagementModule: 8. Dispatch event to UpdateGoalProgressHandler
    EngagementModule->>PrimaryDatabase: 8.1. UPDATE Goals SET Progress = Progress + X
    PrimaryDatabase-->>EngagementModule: Success
    InfrastructureMediatR->>EngagementModule: 9. Dispatch event to UpdateReadingStreakHandler
    activate RecommendationsModule
    InfrastructureMediatR->>RecommendationsModule: 10. Dispatch event to InvalidateUserProfileHandler

    note over EngagementModule: Idempotency: All handlers must be designed to be idempotent. It's possible for an event to be pro...

    deactivate RecommendationsModule
    deactivate EngagementModule
    deactivate ReadingModule
